But the thing you originally asked for hasn't started
Your ask was "right now every mutation is a job… I want to keep React Query mutations clean." My review recommended four things:

✅ Fix jobs.cancel
✅ Typed Handle overload
✅ Delete HandleWithPolicy
❌ The flip — the ~107 progressless Job routes become Query/Action
1–3 were preparation. #4 is the deliverable, and it's untouched. Everything since has been the drift detour that the type check opened up.

Two findings from the original review are still open, and the flip closes most of both
Secrets in job snapshots. No redaction exists; Snapshot.Request still holds the decoded request verbatim for 30 minutes, served by jobs.get/jobs.list/jobs.events. Four routes carry plaintext credentials — and three of them (accounts.change_password, accounts.create_user, storage.mount_cifs) are Job(...).Handle routes the flip turns into Query, which deletes the exposure rather than redacting it. Only virt.create needs real redaction, because it genuinely emits progress. (The result-side twin of this — the wireguard private key — is fixed.)

B7, the one confirmed correctness bug: router.go still takes the goroutine path whenever policy.Timeout > 0, and ActionDefault.Timeout is 120 min — so on cancel the select returns, the job goes terminal, finishJob promotes the next queued job, and the handler goroutine is still executing. Real concurrency exceeds MaxActivePerRoute. This applies to every handler-form job route today; the flip removes it for the ~107 that stop being jobs.

What I'd do next
Start the flip, batched by handler. First batch: accounts — 12 of its 15 routes are already typed, it contains two of the four credential routes, nothing in it emits progress, and nothing plausibly depends on job semantics.

Three questions per route, and they're the actual work:

Does it rely on ActionDefault's accidental serialization? (MaxActivePerOwnerRoute: 1) — decide explicitly rather than inherit it.
Is it self-severing? control.reboot/power_off/logoff and network.set_ipv4* destroy the connection by design; those need the plan's expected_loss/native_handoff treatment before Query mode is safe. Not in batch one.
Call-site change — useJobAction → useAction for that handler's routes.

